# Default session — startup layout
#
# Applied by config/sway/config, which is the config every sway entry on the
# login screen loads except Sway(fonn): "Sway", "Sway 1.11" and "Sway (Nvidia)".
# Sway (Nvidia) is the one you actually log into, so this is that desk.
#
# One line per app:   <workspace number>   <command>
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Everything after the first token is
# the command, run through a shell, so flags / pipes / $HOME all work.
#
# A workspace number may repeat — that is how a screen gets split between two
# apps. They open left to right in the order listed here.
#
# Use `-` instead of a number for an app that should NOT own a screen. Those are
# started last, after the numbered screens are placed, so a window on its way to
# the scratchpad can't be mistaken for a screen's app arriving.
#
# Screens open in order. sway-layout switches to the workspace BEFORE launching
# and waits for the window to appear before moving on — that is what puts each
# app on the right screen without identifying windows by app_id or class, which
# is brittle here: Slack, Discord and TickTick are XWayland, Slack, Discord and
# Obsidian are flatpaks, and ghostty refuses to start if --class isn't
# reverse-DNS.
#
# A slot that already holds a window is left alone, so re-running this
# mid-session won't open a second copy of anything.

1   ghostty

# Zen lives in ~/.local/bin, which sway's PATH at login does not have —
# sway-layout prepends it. No Space is forced here the way fonn.layout forces
# CareerPlug: this desk opens Zen wherever you left it.
2   zen

# Screen 3, split: Discord left, Slack right.
#
# The `slack` on PATH is the snap (/snap/bin/slack). It starts a process but
# never maps a window on this machine — that is why `exec slack` in the old
# config never actually gave you Slack. The flatpak build works, so use it.
3   flatpak run com.discordapp.Discord
3   flatpak run com.slack.Slack

# Screen 4, split: TickTick left, Spotify right.
#
# TickTick only stays here because the scratchpad rule for it lives in
# fonn.config now rather than in common — see the note there.
4   ticktick
4   spotify

5   flatpak run md.obsidian.Obsidian

# Scratchpad apps — no screen of their own. Mod+minus summons the last one.
-   thunderbird
